  "description": "Client for AuthService's public human-facing session endpoints (contract §4.2-§4.4): login/request, login/verify, refresh, logout. Counterpart to Concierge.Auth.Client.AuthGuard, which validates a token someone else issued — this is how a client service obtains one. No DbContext, no credential store, no encryption key, and no ProjectReference on the base package: these are public human endpoints, none of the other five packages' persistence machinery applies. Ships a pluggable ISessionTokenStore plus a cookie implementation; contract §9 open item #16 (cookie vs header storage) is deliberately left unresolved.",
